#: ../../library/vfs.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`vfs` --- virtual filesystem control"
msgstr ":mod:`vfs` --- upravljanje virtualnim datotečnim sustavom"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:7
msgid ""
"The ``vfs`` module contains functions for creating filesystem objects and "
"mounting/unmounting them in the Virtual Filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Modul ``vfs`` sadrži funkcije za stvaranje objekata datotečnog sustava te "
"njihovo montiranje i odmontiranje u virtualnom datotečnom sustavu (Virtual "
"Filesystem)."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:11
msgid "Filesystem mounting"
msgstr "Montiranje datotečnog sustava"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:13
msgid ""
"Some ports provide a Virtual Filesystem (VFS) and the ability to mount "
"multiple \"real\" filesystems within this VFS.  Filesystem objects can be "
"mounted at either the root of the VFS, or at a subdirectory that lives in "
"the root.  This allows dynamic and flexible configuration of the filesystem "
"that is seen by Python programs.  Ports that have this functionality provide"
" the :func:`mount` and :func:`umount` functions, and possibly various "
"filesystem implementations represented by VFS classes."
msgstr ""
"Neki portovi pružaju virtualni datotečni sustav (VFS) i mogućnost montiranja"
" više \"stvarnih\" datotečnih sustava unutar tog VFS-a. Objekti datotečnog "
"sustava mogu se montirati ili u korijenu VFS-a ili u poddirektoriju koji se "
"nalazi u korijenu. To omogućuje dinamičku i fleksibilnu konfiguraciju "
"datotečnog sustava koji vide Python programi. Portovi koji imaju ovu "
"funkcionalnost pružaju funkcije :func:`mount` i :func:`umount`\\ , a moguće "
"i razne implementacije datotečnih sustava predstavljene VFS klasama."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:23
msgid ""
"Mount the filesystem object *fsobj* at the location in the VFS given by the "
"*mount_point* string.  *fsobj* can be a a VFS object that has a ``mount()`` "
"method, or a block device.  If it's a block device then the filesystem type "
"is automatically detected (an exception is raised if no filesystem was "
"recognised).  *mount_point* may be ``'/'`` to mount *fsobj* at the root, or "
"``'/<name>'`` to mount it at a subdirectory under the root."
msgstr ""
"Montira objekt datotečnog sustava *fsobj* na lokaciju u VFS-u zadanu nizom "
"*mount_point*\\ . *fsobj* može biti VFS objekt koji ima metodu ``mount()`` "
"ili blok uređaj. Ako je riječ o blok uređaju, tip datotečnog sustava se "
"automatski prepoznaje (podiže se iznimka ako nijedan datotečni sustav nije "
"prepoznat). *mount_point* može biti ``'/'`` za montiranje *fsobj* u korijenu"
" ili ``'/<name>'`` za montiranje u poddirektoriju ispod korijena."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:30
msgid "If *readonly* is ``True`` then the filesystem is mounted read-only."
msgstr ""
"Ako je *readonly* postavljen na ``True``\\ , datotečni sustav se montira "
"samo za čitanje."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:32
msgid ""
"During the mount process the method ``mount()`` is called on the filesystem "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Tijekom postupka montiranja na objektu datotečnog sustava poziva se metoda "
"``mount()``\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:35
msgid "Will raise ``OSError(EPERM)`` if *mount_point* is already mounted."
msgstr "Podiže ``OSError(EPERM)`` ako je *mount_point* već montiran."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:40
msgid ""
"With no arguments to :func:`mount`, return a list of tuples representing all"
" active mountpoints."
msgstr ""
"Bez argumenata, :func:`mount` vraća popis n-torki koje predstavljaju sve "
"aktivne točke montiranja."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:43
msgid "The returned list has the form *[(fsobj, mount_point), ...]*."
msgstr "Vraćeni popis ima oblik *[(fsobj, mount_point), ...]*\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:47
msgid ""
"Unmount a filesystem. *mount_point* can be a string naming the mount "
"location, or a previously-mounted filesystem object.  During the unmount "
"process the method ``umount()`` is called on the filesystem object."
msgstr ""
"Odmontira datotečni sustav. *mount_point* može biti niz koji imenuje "
"lokaciju montiranja ili prethodno montirani objekt datotečnog sustava. "
"Tijekom postupka odmontiranja na objektu datotečnog sustava poziva se metoda"
" ``umount()``\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:51
msgid "Will raise ``OSError(EINVAL)`` if *mount_point* is not found."
msgstr "Podiže ``OSError(EINVAL)`` ako *mount_point* nije pronađen."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:55
msgid ""
"Create a filesystem object that uses the FAT filesystem format.  Storage of "
"the FAT filesystem is provided by *block_dev*. Objects created by this "
"constructor can be mounted using :func:`mount`."
msgstr ""
"Stvara objekt datotečnog sustava koji koristi format datotečnog sustava FAT."
" Pohranu FAT datotečnog sustava pruža *block_dev*\\ . Objekti stvoreni ovim "
"konstruktorom mogu se montirati pomoću :func:`mount`\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:61
msgid "Build a FAT filesystem on *block_dev*."
msgstr "Izgrađuje FAT datotečni sustav na *block_dev*\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:65
msgid ""
"Create a filesystem object that uses the :ref:`ROMFS read-only filesystem "
"format <romfs>`. ``buffer`` must be an object supporting the buffer protocol"
" (``bytes``, ``bytearray`` or ``memoryview``) that contains a valid ROMFS "
"image."
msgstr ""
"Stvara objekt datotečnog sustava koji koristi :ref:`ROMFS format datotečnog "
"sustava samo za čitanje <romfs>`\\ . ``buffer`` mora biti objekt koji "
"podržava protokol međuspremnika (\\ ``bytes``\\ , ``bytearray`` ili "
"``memoryview``\\ ) i koji sadrži valjanu ROMFS sliku."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:70
msgid ""
"Objects created by this constructor can be mounted using :func:`mount`."
msgstr ""
"Objekti stvoreni ovim konstruktorom mogu se montirati pomoću :func:`mount`\\"
" ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:72
msgid ""
"See :ref:`romfs` for full details, including how to build and deploy ROMFS "
"images with :ref:`mpremote <mpremote>`."
msgstr ""
"Za sve pojedinosti, uključujući kako izgraditi i postaviti ROMFS slike "
"pomoću :ref:`mpremote <mpremote>`\\ , pogledajte :ref:`romfs`\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:77
msgid ""
"Low-level interface for accessing the read-only memory (ROM) partition(s) of"
" the device. The supported operations are:"
msgstr ""
"Niskorazinsko sučelje za pristup particijama memorije samo za čitanje (ROM) "
"uređaja. Podržane operacije su:"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:84
msgid "Call"
msgstr "Poziv"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:85
msgid "Behaviour"
msgstr "Ponašanje"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:86
msgid "``rom_ioctl(1)``"
msgstr "``rom_ioctl(1)``"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:87
msgid "Return the number of available ROM partitions."
msgstr "Vraća broj dostupnih ROM particija."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:88
msgid "``rom_ioctl(2, id)``"
msgstr "``rom_ioctl(2, id)``"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:89
msgid "Return partition ``id`` as a ``memoryview``."
msgstr "Vraća particiju ``id`` kao ``memoryview``\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:90
msgid "``rom_ioctl(3, id, length)``"
msgstr "``rom_ioctl(3, id, length)``"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:91
msgid ""
"Erase the first ``length`` bytes of partition ``id`` in preparation for "
"writing. Returns the minimum write alignment in bytes."
msgstr ""
"Briše prvih ``length`` bajtova particije ``id`` u pripremi za pisanje. Vraća"
" minimalno poravnanje za pisanje u bajtovima."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:94
msgid "``rom_ioctl(4, id, offset, buf)``"
msgstr "``rom_ioctl(4, id, offset, buf)``"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:95
msgid "Write ``buf`` to partition ``id`` at byte ``offset``."
msgstr "Zapisuje ``buf`` u particiju ``id`` na bajt ``offset``\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:96
msgid "``rom_ioctl(5, id)``"
msgstr "``rom_ioctl(5, id)``"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:97
msgid "Finalise a write sequence to partition ``id`` (flushes caches, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Finalizira slijed pisanja u particiju ``id`` (prazni predmemorije itd.)."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:100
msgid ""
"These operations are normally invoked indirectly by :ref:`mpremote "
"<mpremote>` when deploying a ROMFS image; most applications do not need to "
"call them directly."
msgstr ""
"Te operacije obično neizravno poziva :ref:`mpremote <mpremote>` prilikom "
"postavljanja ROMFS slike; većina aplikacija ih ne treba pozivati izravno."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:106
msgid ""
"Create a filesystem object that accesses the host POSIX filesystem. If "
"*root* is specified then it should be a path in the host filesystem to use "
"as the root of the ``VfsPosix`` object.  Otherwise the current directory of "
"the host filesystem is used."
msgstr ""
"Stvara objekt datotečnog sustava koji pristupa POSIX datotečnom sustavu "
"domaćina. Ako je *root* naveden, treba biti putanja u datotečnom sustavu "
"domaćina koja se koristi kao korijen ``VfsPosix`` objekta. Inače se koristi "
"trenutni direktorij datotečnog sustava domaćina."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:113
msgid ""
":class:`VfsPosix` is only available on the MicroPython Unix port; it is not "
"present in OpenMV Cam firmware."
msgstr ""
":class:`VfsPosix` je dostupan samo na MicroPython Unix portu; nije prisutan "
"u ugrađenom programu (firmware) OpenMV Cam-a."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:117
msgid "Block devices"
msgstr "Blok uređaji"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:119
msgid ""
"A block device is an object which implements the block protocol. This "
"enables a device to support MicroPython filesystems. The physical hardware "
"is represented by a user defined class. The :class:`AbstractBlockDev` class "
"is a template for the design of such a class: MicroPython does not actually "
"provide that class, but an actual block device class must implement the "
"methods described below."
msgstr ""
"Blok uređaj je objekt koji implementira protokol blokova. To omogućuje "
"uređaju da podržava MicroPython datotečne sustave. Fizički hardver "
"predstavlja korisnički definirana klasa. Klasa :class:`AbstractBlockDev` je "
"predložak za dizajn takve klase: MicroPython tu klasu zapravo ne pruža, ali "
"stvarna klasa blok uređaja mora implementirati metode opisane u nastavku."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:125
msgid ""
"A concrete implementation of this class will usually allow access to the "
"memory-like functionality of a piece of hardware (like flash memory). A "
"block device can be formatted to any supported filesystem and mounted using "
"``os`` methods."
msgstr ""
"Konkretna implementacija ove klase obično omogućuje pristup funkcionalnosti "
"sličnoj memoriji nekog dijela hardvera (poput flash memorije). Blok uređaj "
"može se formatirati u bilo koji podržani datotečni sustav i montirati pomoću"
" metoda ``os``\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:130
msgid ""
"See :ref:`filesystem` for example implementations of block devices using the"
" two variants of the block protocol described below."
msgstr ""
"Pogledajte :ref:`filesystem` za primjere implementacija blok uređaja pomoću "
"dvije varijante protokola blokova opisane u nastavku."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:136
msgid "Simple and extended interface"
msgstr "Jednostavno i prošireno sučelje"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:138
msgid ""
"There are two compatible signatures for the ``readblocks`` and "
"``writeblocks`` methods (see below), in order to support a variety of use "
"cases.  A given block device may implement one form or the other, or both at"
" the same time. The second form (with the offset parameter) is referred to "
"as the \"extended interface\"."
msgstr ""
"Postoje dva kompatibilna potpisa za metode ``readblocks`` i ``writeblocks`` "
"(vidi dolje), kako bi se podržali razni slučajevi upotrebe. Određeni blok "
"uređaj može implementirati jedan ili drugi oblik, ili oba istovremeno. Drugi"
" oblik (s parametrom offset) naziva se \"prošireno sučelje\"."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:143
msgid ""
"Some filesystems require more control over write operations -- for example, "
"writing to sub-block regions without erasing -- and need the block device to"
" support the extended interface."
msgstr ""
"Neki datotečni sustavi zahtijevaju veću kontrolu nad operacijama pisanja -- "
"na primjer, pisanje u podregije bloka bez brisanja -- te zahtijevaju da blok"
" uređaj podržava prošireno sučelje."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:149
msgid ""
"Documentation template for the block-device protocol. MicroPython does not "
"actually expose this class --- it is shown here only to document the methods"
" a user-defined block-device class must implement. Constructor arguments are"
" entirely up to the implementation (typically things like flash bus, chip-"
"select pin, sector size, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Predložak dokumentacije za protokol blok uređaja. MicroPython zapravo ne "
"izlaže ovu klasu --- ovdje je prikazana samo radi dokumentiranja metoda koje"
" korisnički definirana klasa blok uređaja mora implementirati. Argumenti "
"konstruktora u potpunosti ovise o implementaciji (obično stvari poput flash "
"sabirnice, pina za odabir čipa, veličine sektora itd.)."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:158
msgid ""
"Read bytes from the device into *buf*. Two overloads expose the :ref:`simple"
" and extended <block-device-interface>` interfaces."
msgstr ""
"Čita bajtove s uređaja u *buf*\\ . Dvije preopterećene varijante izlažu "
":ref:`jednostavno i prošireno <block-device-interface>` sučelje."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:161
msgid ""
"**Simple form** (``readblocks(block_num, buf)``): reads whole blocks "
"starting at block index *block_num*. ``len(buf)`` must be a multiple of the "
"block size, and the number of blocks read is ``len(buf) // block_size``."
msgstr ""
"**Jednostavni oblik** (\\ ``readblocks(block_num, buf)``\\ ): čita cijele "
"blokove počevši od indeksa bloka *block_num*\\ . ``len(buf)`` mora biti "
"višekratnik veličine bloka, a broj pročitanih blokova je ``len(buf) // "
"block_size``\\ ."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:166
msgid ""
"**Extended form** (``readblocks(block_num, buf, offset)``): reads "
"``len(buf)`` bytes -- not necessarily a whole number of blocks -- starting "
"at byte ``offset`` within block *block_num*. Use this form when the "
"filesystem needs sub-block read access."
msgstr ""
"**Prošireni oblik** (\\ ``readblocks(block_num, buf, offset)``\\ ): čita "
"``len(buf)`` bajtova -- ne nužno cijeli broj blokova -- počevši od bajta "
"``offset`` unutar bloka *block_num*\\ . Koristite ovaj oblik kada datotečni "
"sustav treba pristup čitanju unutar bloka."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:174
msgid "Write bytes from *buf* to the device."
msgstr "Zapisuje bajtove iz *buf* na uređaj."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:176
msgid ""
"**Simple form** (``writeblocks(block_num, buf)``): writes whole blocks "
"starting at block index *block_num*. ``len(buf)`` must be a multiple of the "
"block size, and the number of blocks written is ``len(buf) // block_size``. "
"The implementation is responsible for erasing each destination block first "
"if the underlying hardware requires it."
msgstr ""
"**Jednostavni oblik** (\\ ``writeblocks(block_num, buf)``\\ ): zapisuje "
"cijele blokove počevši od indeksa bloka *block_num*\\ . ``len(buf)`` mora "
"biti višekratnik veličine bloka, a broj zapisanih blokova je ``len(buf) // "
"block_size``\\ . Implementacija je odgovorna za prethodno brisanje svakog "
"odredišnog bloka ako to zahtijeva osnovni hardver."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:183
msgid ""
"**Extended form** (``writeblocks(block_num, buf, offset)``): writes "
"``len(buf)`` bytes -- not necessarily a whole number of blocks -- starting "
"at byte ``offset`` within block *block_num*. Only the bytes being written "
"may change; the caller is responsible for ensuring affected blocks have been"
" erased via a prior :meth:`ioctl(6, block_num) <ioctl>` call. "
"Implementations of this form **must never** implicitly erase a block, even "
"when ``offset`` is zero."
msgstr ""
"**Prošireni oblik** (\\ ``writeblocks(block_num, buf, offset)``\\ ): "
"zapisuje ``len(buf)`` bajtova -- ne nužno cijeli broj blokova -- počevši od "
"bajta ``offset`` unutar bloka *block_num*\\ . Mijenjaju se samo bajtovi koji"
" se zapisuju; pozivatelj je odgovoran za osiguravanje da su zahvaćeni "
"blokovi obrisani prethodnim pozivom :meth:`ioctl(6, block_num) <ioctl>`\\ . "
"Implementacije ovog oblika **nikada ne smiju** implicitno obrisati blok, čak"
" ni kada je ``offset`` jednak nuli."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:194
msgid ""
"Control the block device and query its parameters.  The operation to perform"
" is given by *op* which is one of the following integers:"
msgstr ""
"Upravlja blok uređajem i ispituje njegove parametre. Operacija koja se "
"izvodi zadana je s *op*\\ , što je jedan od sljedećih cijelih brojeva:"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:197
msgid "1 -- initialise the device (*arg* is unused)"
msgstr "1 -- inicijalizacija uređaja (\\ *arg* se ne koristi)"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:198
msgid "2 -- shutdown the device (*arg* is unused)"
msgstr "2 -- gašenje uređaja (\\ *arg* se ne koristi)"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:199
msgid "3 -- sync the device (*arg* is unused)"
msgstr "3 -- sinkronizacija uređaja (\\ *arg* se ne koristi)"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:200
msgid ""
"4 -- get a count of the number of blocks, should return an integer (*arg* is"
" unused)"
msgstr ""
"4 -- dohvat broja blokova, treba vratiti cijeli broj (\\ *arg* se ne "
"koristi)"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:202
msgid ""
"5 -- get the number of bytes in a block, should return an integer, or "
"``None`` in which case the default value of 512 is used (*arg* is unused)"
msgstr ""
"5 -- dohvat broja bajtova u bloku, treba vratiti cijeli broj ili ``None`` u "
"kojem se slučaju koristi zadana vrijednost 512 (\\ *arg* se ne koristi)"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:205
msgid "6 -- erase a block, *arg* is the block number to erase"
msgstr "6 -- brisanje bloka, *arg* je broj bloka koji se briše"

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:207
msgid ""
"As a minimum ``ioctl(4, ...)`` must be intercepted; filesystems that use the"
" extended interface additionally require ``ioctl(6, ...)``. The need for the"
" other operations is hardware-dependent."
msgstr ""
"Kao minimum mora se presresti ``ioctl(4, ...)``\\ ; datotečni sustavi koji "
"koriste prošireno sučelje dodatno zahtijevaju ``ioctl(6, ...)``\\ . Potreba "
"za ostalim operacijama ovisi o hardveru."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:211
msgid ""
"Before any call to ``writeblocks(block, ...)`` a filesystem that uses the "
"extended interface issues ``ioctl(6, block)`` so the driver can erase the "
"block first if the hardware requires it. A driver may instead intercept "
"``ioctl(6, block)`` and return 0 (success), taking on the responsibility for"
" detecting when erasure is needed itself."
msgstr ""
"Prije svakog poziva ``writeblocks(block, ...)`` datotečni sustav koji "
"koristi prošireno sučelje izdaje ``ioctl(6, block)`` kako bi upravljački "
"program prvo obrisao blok ako to hardver zahtijeva. Upravljački program može"
" umjesto toga presresti ``ioctl(6, block)`` i vratiti 0 (uspjeh), "
"preuzimajući na sebe odgovornost za samostalno otkrivanje kada je brisanje "
"potrebno."

#: ../../library/vfs.rst:217
msgid ""
"Unless otherwise stated ``ioctl(op, arg)`` can return ``None``. Consequently"
" an implementation can ignore unused values of ``op``. Where ``op`` is "
"intercepted, the return value for operations 4 and 5 are as detailed above. "
"Other operations should return 0 on success and non-zero for failure, with "
"the value returned being an ``OSError`` errno code."
msgstr ""
"Osim ako nije drugačije navedeno, ``ioctl(op, arg)`` može vratiti ``None``\\"
" . Slijedom toga, implementacija može zanemariti nekorištene vrijednosti za "
"``op``\\ . Tamo gdje se ``op`` presreće, povratna vrijednost za operacije 4 "
"i 5 je kako je gore detaljno opisano. Ostale operacije trebaju vratiti 0 u "
"slučaju uspjeha i različito od nule u slučaju neuspjeha, pri čemu je vraćena"
" vrijednost ``OSError`` errno kod."
